---
layout: base.njk
---
<section class="hero">
  <div class="eyebrow">{{ site.role }}</div>
  <h1>Hi, I'm {{ site.shortName }}.<br>I make data you can trust, and see.</h1>
  <p class="lede">{{ site.tagline }} Everything on this site is live: it pulls real news data every morning, rebuilds itself, and publishes, with nobody touching it.</p>
  <div class="actions">
    <a class="btn primary" href="#dashboards">Explore the dashboards</a>
    <a class="btn" href="/about/">What I can build for you</a>
  </div>
</section>

<section aria-label="Today in numbers">
  <div class="grid three">
    <div class="card stat">
      <div class="value">{{ bbc.totalStories | num }}</div>
      <div class="label">BBC stories tracked across {{ bbc.sections.length }} sections</div>
    </div>
    <div class="card stat">
      <div class="value">{% if insights.leader %}{{ insights.leader.last.toFixed(2) }}%{% else %}n/a{% endif %}</div>
      <div class="label">of global news coverage is about <b>{{ insights.leader.label }}</b>, the top topic we track</div>
    </div>
    <div class="card stat">
      <div class="value">{{ hn.stories[0].points | num }}</div>
      <div class="label">points on today's top Hacker News story</div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="muted">Data last refreshed {{ bbc.updated | when }}.</p>
</section>

<section id="dashboards">
  <h2>Dashboards</h2>
  <div class="grid three">
    <a class="card" href="/dashboards/global-coverage/">
      <h3>What the world is talking about</h3>
      <p class="muted">Share of global news coverage for {{ gdelt.topics.length }} big topics over the last three months, from the GDELT Project.</p>
      <span class="go">Open dashboard →</span>
    </a>
    <a class="card" href="/dashboards/headlines/">
      <h3>Today's headlines, by the numbers</h3>
      <p class="muted">Which BBC News sections are busiest, and the words dominating today's headlines.</p>
      <span class="go">Open dashboard →</span>
    </a>
    <a class="card" href="/dashboards/tech/">
      <h3>What tech is reading</h3>
      <p class="muted">The most upvoted stories on the Hacker News front page right now.</p>
      <span class="go">Open dashboard →</span>
    </a>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>How this site runs itself</h2>
  <p class="muted">The same pattern I use for automated test pipelines: scheduled, self-checking, zero cost.</p>
  <ol class="steps">
    <li><b>Schedule</b>A GitHub Action wakes up every morning.</li>
    <li><b>Collect</b>A Node script pulls GDELT, BBC and Hacker News data, with retries and fallbacks.</li>
    <li><b>Build</b>Eleventy turns the data into static pages and charts.</li>
    <li><b>Publish</b>GitHub Pages serves it free. If a source is down, yesterday's data stays up.</li>
  </ol>
</section>
